Package: csls
Title: Criminology and Sociolegal Statistics
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person(c("Vansh", "Singh"), "Ruhela", email = "vsruhela@proton.me",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0004-1750-3592"))
Description: Statistical methods for courts, corrections, policing,
    forensics and sociolegal research, computed in a compiled core with a
    thin R layer.
    Each identity or bound the package relies on names the machine-checked
    proof ('Lean') it rests on. This development version holds the disparity
    tests: the veil-of-darkness contrast of Grogger and Ridgeway (2006)
    <doi:10.1198/016214506000000168>, the outcome test and its
    infra-marginality problem, benchmark decomposition of resident
    disparities, dyadic offending rates, and the bounds a relative risk
    obeys given an odds ratio.
